Order inside one block follows emotion: the block's own declarations come
first, in source order, then its nested rules (pseudo-classes, `@media`,
selectors), in source order. The same holds inside each nested rule.

`mediaFirst` writes `@media { color: pink }` before `color: black`, so pink
applies under the media query. `familySpansMedia` groups `padding: 8px` and
`padding-top: 0` into one atom; the group comes before the `@media` rule, so
`padding: 16px` applies at 768px and wider. In `card`, the `_in_` bundle
holds the base and `:focus` rules; `:focus` is written last, so it comes
after `:hover`. In `nested`, the `:hover` rule's own `margin: 8px` comes
before its `@media` rule.

